 This is a non-renewable post open for the specific needs of a National Project, for a duration of 4 years, that pending upon performance and project extension, may be extended up to a possible maximum duration of 8 years.  Accordingly, the external candidate selected for this post will continue to be considered an external candidate for the purposes of any future applications to the Agency. 
 Location 
ESOC, Darmstadt, Germany or ESAC, Villanueva de la Cañada, Spain
 Description 
 Radar Engineer in the Ground-based Communication and Tracking Assets Section (OPS-GSA), reporting to the Head of Section in the Ground Station Engineering Division.
 You will contribute to the development of the radar and phased-array subsystem, and you will provide functional support to the Greek Radar project.
 Duties 
 You will be in charge of the development and engineering activities related to ground-based radars for surveillance and tracking applications, including radar system and sub-system design, procurement and assembly, integration and on-site validation.
 Your tasks and responsibilities will include:
 supporting the procurement of the Greek Radar project;
 ingpecifying, developing, procuring and validating radar and phased-array subsystems, including trade-off analyses;
 supporting radar and phased-array research and development activities;
 conducting internal and external studies and prototyping activities in the area of radar and phased-array subsystems;
 managing related industrial contracts.
 Technical competencies 
 Radar system and subsystem engineering Signal and Data Processing Testing and validation of radar systems and subsystems Phased-array subsystem engineering Knowledge of one or more programming languages to simulate radar systems and subsystems (MATLAB, Python or similar) Site infrastructure requirements for radar systems and phased-array antennas Behavioural competencies 
 Result Orientation
Operational Efficiency
Fostering Cooperation
Relationship Management
Continuous Improvement
Forward Thinking
For more information, please refer to ESA Core Behavioural Competencies guidebook 
 Education and professional experience 
 A master's degree in a relevant domain is required for this post together with 10 years of relevant professional experience.
 Additional requirements 
 You should have proven experience in radar, phased-array design and development. Experience in project management will be an asset. You should demonstrate strong motivation, the ability to define solutions and solve problems autonomously, and the ability to communicate effectively within both the project team and the wider organization.
 Diversity, Equity and Inclusiveness  
ESA is an equal opportunity employer, committed to achieving diversity within the workforce and creating an inclusive working environment. We therefore welcome applications from all qualified candidates irrespective of gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religious beliefs, age, disability or other characteristics. 
 At the Agency we value diversity, and we welcome people with disabilities. Whenever possible, we seek to accommodate individuals with disabilities by providing the necessary support at the workplace. The Human Resources Department can also provide assistance during the recruitment process. If you would like to discuss this further, please contact us via email at contact.human.resources@esa.int .
 Important Information and Disclaimer 
In principle, recruitment will be within the advertised grade band (A2-A4). However, if the selected candidate has less than four years of relevant professional experience following the completion of the master’s degree, the position may be filled at A1 level.
 During the recruitment process, the Agency may request applicants to undergo selection tests. Additionally, successful candidates will need to undergo basic screening before appointment, which will be conducted by an external background screening service, in compliance with the European Space Agency's security procedures.
 Note that ESA is in the process of transitioning to a Matrix setup, which could lead to organisational changes affecting this position.
 The information published on ESA’s careers website regarding working conditions is correct at the time of publication. It is not intended to be exhaustive and may not address all questions you would have. 
 Nationality and Languages  Please note that applications are only considered from nationals of one of the following States: Austria, Belgium, Czechia, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and Canada, Cyprus, Latvia, Lithuania and Slovakia.
 According to the ESA Convention, staff shall be recruited on the basis of their qualifications, taking into account an adequate distribution of posts among nationals of the Member States.
 The working languages of the Agency are English and French. A good knowledge of one of these is required. Knowledge of another Member State language would be an asset.  
